# The Dockerfile runs `npm ci` and only then copies the source. Without this
# file, that copy overwrites the freshly installed node_modules with the host's
# — built on AlmaLinux against glibc, landing in an Alpine image that uses musl.
# Nothing native is installed today, so nothing breaks today; the day something
# is, it breaks in a way that reads as a code bug rather than a packaging one.
node_modules

# Build output and test artefacts. Regenerated inside the image, and copying
# them in only makes the context larger and the layer staler.
.next
out
test-results
playwright-report
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

.git
.gitignore
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store

# Local environment files. These would otherwise be baked into an image layer,
# where a secret survives every later deletion.
.env
.env.*
